# Zod schemas

- Put request bodies in `*.schema.ts` next to the feature
- Use Zod + `createZodDto` from `nestjs-zod`
- CamelCase fields (`bodyText`, `closeNote`, `qrToken`)
- Rely on the global `ZodValidationPipe` in `main.ts` — do not add class-validator or per-route validation pipes

```typescript
import { createZodDto } from 'nestjs-zod';
import { z } from 'zod';

export const CreateThingSchema = z.object({
  bodyText: z.string().trim().min(1).max(2000),
});
export class CreateThingDto extends createZodDto(CreateThingSchema) {}
```

Unit-test schemas with `safeParse` in `tests/*.spec.ts`.
